                           S I C K     C H A T 
          - - ---------------------------------------------- - -

                            By ZEd Of CDTE-SoFT


Purpose:
~~~~~~~~
	Replace DayDream's internal split screen chatter with a more
featureful one. Much like ICE-Chat on the IBM, but better! :)



Features:
~~~~~~~~~
- Split Screen
- Partial Screen Scroll
- Real time moving clock at bottom
- Chat timer at bottom
- CTRL-Z gives you a temporary line chat
- Macros
- Different colors for different character types
  (letters, numbers, etc)
- CTRL-L only clears your chat window and not the user's.
- SysOp can swap windows with user by pressing CTRL-S
- CTRL-R redraws the screen
- Function Keys
- Can be configured to look like you want it!
- Alot more, you'll have to try it out, or look at the Preview pics.



Installation:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	Copy SICK-CHAT into doors:, then copy all Display/ISO/ files
included in this archive into your ansi directory. Then run MUICONFIG
and set chat type to "DOOR" and in the CHATDOOR text field put 
"Doors:Sick-Chat %N". Hit AMIGA - and it will load Sick Chat.


SiCK-CHAT.FKeys:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	This file assigns strings (text) to your F-Keys. It simply
goes down the page, the first line being for F1 and last line for F10.
Just edit it with a normal text editor.


Macros:
~~~~~~~
	An example macro file is included. Sick-Chat.Macros goes into
DayDream:Configs/. The structure is as follows:

NUMBER OF MACROS
STRING TO DETECT
REPLACEMENT STRING

Example:

1
BBS
Bulletin Board

 With the above config, if a user types "BBS", "Bulletin Board" will appear
instead. No real practical use for this feature, but it looks good :)



Customizing The Look:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
	To make SiCKCHaT look like you want it, edit SC-XXX.GFX and
Sick-chat.cfg. SC-Top.GFX is the bar above the sysop's window and
SC-Mid.gfx is the one in the middle etc. Don't put any positioning
codes in these ansis, ie ^[[x;yH, this should be done in SiCK-CHaT.CFG.
If you want to make SiCK-CHaT look like the old version, use the config
and ansi's found in the oldconfig/ directory.



Note:
~~~~~
	The door can do strange things to DayDream if you run it before the
user has got the main menu (while in WELCOME.GFX). So just don't do it :)



